Prefarably, carve the E word and put'em in the countainer.  I like having
them on the 'branch level'.

Carving E word will protect the pile from being walked all over by hostile
monster and them picking up stuff, using them against you.  E word does not
protect it against peaceful monster walking into the pile and picking up the
stuff, so you need to put'em into a container (They don't go into the
container, and if you put enough stuff into the container, it'll be too
heavy to pick up).  It'll be pretty safe and secure then.

As for the level, I like the level that has branching.  The Dungeon of Doom
level where there are:

Stairs to Mines
Stairs to Sokoban
Quest Entrance

I also like to have my camp right next to the co-aligned alter.  I can check
the BUC status of the item and then immediately stash'em away.  Plus items
that generate monsters can be used right next to it for convenient
sacrificing.  Also they tend to drop items.  And also potions can be turned
into water than blessed right there.

My latest game has a camp right next to the co-aligned alter and quest
entrance...

